# Caddy site block for fusionlocalserver — merge into /etc/caddy/Caddyfile and
# replace the hostname with your real subdomain (the same one in PUBLIC_URL and
# the APS callback registration).
#
# Caddy obtains and renews the Let's Encrypt certificate automatically (the DNS
# A record must already point here and ports 80/443 must be open), redirects
# HTTP to HTTPS, preserves the Host header, and sets X-Forwarded-Proto/-For —
# which the app uses to mark its session cookie Secure, emit HSTS, and key its
# per-IP auth rate limiter on the real client rather than on the proxy. The app
# itself listens on plain-HTTP :8080 (no -tls) and stays firewalled from the
# internet.
#
# Those forwarded headers are honored only from a trusted peer, and loopback is
# always trusted — so proxying from this same VM needs nothing extra. A proxy on
# another host must be named with the app's -trusted-proxy flag.
#
# If you change the app's port in Settings, update the target here too —
# otherwise Caddy keeps proxying to a port nothing listens on.

fls.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
